# ONE local folder is still ignored here. `.memory/` and `.workgroup/` moved to the workbench
# home at `~/.workbench/<org>/` on 2026-09-16 and are no longer in this tree, so their rules were
# removed rather than left behind: this file's own lesson (below) is that an ignore rule is not
# the same as absence, and keeping a rule for a directory that cannot appear describes the tree
# wrongly. `.profile/` has not moved -- its destination is a separate private operator repository
# -- so it is still a real directory here and still must never be committed.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, git matches the name at ANY depth
# and silently swallowed templates/layout/, whose whole purpose is to be committed and
# handed to an adopter. The failure was invisible until something checked.
/.profile/

# Employer-specific discipline USED to be ignored here. It is not any more -- it moved to
# `~/.workbench/<org>/foundations/` on 2026-09-16, so there is nothing to hide and no rule
# to write. The lesson is worth keeping: an ignore rule in a public repository is itself
# published, so a rule naming the org leaks the identifier the folder exists to protect.
# Ignoring something is not the same as it being absent, and only the second is private.

# Agent scratchpad. Declared here rather than globally, for the same reason as above.
# Unrelated to the moved `.memory/` store -- this is the `<topic>.memory.md` file convention.
*.memory.md

# Recordings are raw material -- bulky, disposable, and full of workspace paths.
# What outlives one is what was distilled out of it, which now lives in the workbench home
# at `~/.workbench/<org>/.memory/`.
observations/
